            <ArticleTitle>Continuous axillary brachial plexus analgesia in a patient with severe hemophilia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>38-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Until now, the safety of continuous axillary brachial plexus block in a patient with hemophilia has not been reported. We describe the use of continuous axillary brachial plexus block for postoperative pain control in a patient with severe hemophilia after an elbow surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
